※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4201

※ There is no `i1`.  A signed type of one bit holds zero and minus one, which
※ is a pair of values no program wants and a name every reader would misread --
※ so the name is not given out, and what a program that writes it is told is
※ that there is no such type.  `u1` is there: nothing and one is a pair
※ programs want constantly.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    held(0u1)

fn held(x: i1) → u6:
    0u6
